=head1 DESCRIPTION

Auto-Tune settings when updating a domain. For more information, see
Auto-Tune for Amazon OpenSearch Service
(https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/auto-tune.html).

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 DesiredState => Str

Whether Auto-Tune is enabled or disabled.


=head2 MaintenanceSchedules => ArrayRef[L<Paws::OpenSearch::AutoTuneMaintenanceSchedule>]

DEPRECATED. Use off-peak window
(https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/off-peak.html)
instead.

A list of maintenance schedules during which Auto-Tune can deploy
changes.


=head2 RollbackOnDisable => Str

When disabling Auto-Tune, specify C<NO_ROLLBACK> to retain all prior
Auto-Tune settings or C<DEFAULT_ROLLBACK> to revert to the OpenSearch
Service defaults. If you specify C<DEFAULT_ROLLBACK>, you must include
a C<MaintenanceSchedule> in the request. Otherwise, OpenSearch Service
is unable to perform the rollback.


=head2 UseOffPeakWindow => Bool

Whether to use the domain's off-peak window
(https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/APIReference/API_OffPeakWindow.html)
to deploy configuration changes on the domain rather than a maintenance
schedule.



